# Explain implementation (cursor-packs)

**CONSTRAINT:** When the agent finishes an implementation or fix that changed project files, or when the user asks what changed / how it was built, MUST Read and follow `.cursor/skills/explain-implementation/SKILL.md` before the final user-facing reply.

- MUST: include the skill’s plain-English explain pass (short answer; what is new as behavior steps; optional same-path and authorship sections).
- MUST NOT: end with only a file list, test status, or “want me to commit?” without that explain pass.
- Enforcement: Before send on an implement/fix turn, confirm the skill was applied to the reply draft.
- Violation: STOP, Read the skill, rewrite the reply, then send.

CORRECT:
```text
Edited contextdigest promote path → final reply uses explain-implementation sections
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
Edited files → “Done. Tests pass. Commit?”
```

Chat voice remains `.cursor/rules/always-rules-01-human-interaction.mdc`. This rule only forces the post-implementation teaching structure.
